test_cv_dual_control_volume -- LaGriT's command dump / control_volume (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_control_volume_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]   11 cases, about 2 s
  open summary.html

  (cv_dual is the one beside lagrit: build/cv_dual)

WHAT IS TESTED

  dump / control_volume / mo_name / keyword, value / ... runs cv_dual
  (src/cv_dual) on a mesh object, through src/dump_control_volume.f90
  and the entry point cv_dual_lagrit_entry, with the mesh object's
  own arrays. Each case is a LaGriT deck, NAME.lgi, run in work/NAME;
  the deck writes the mesh with dump / avs (mesh.inp) before the
  command, and again after it (after.inp). Then the cv_dual program
  runs on mesh.inp in work/NAME/prog with the same options (the
  case's program arguments in cases.txt).

  Cases that must work (cv01 ... cv09): tets (a moved lattice, the
  Poisson mesh of test_poisson_3d case 1), 2D triangles, a dfnWorks
  fracture network, two materials; every output format, voronoi,
  median and hybrid control volumes, ParaView and matrix files, a box
  subset (six numbers in the command), zero_tol as a real, check_only,
  attribute_cv_volume with and without a name, and parent/child
  chains (settets / parents) refused, then resetpts / parent and
  rmpoint / compress and the same command working; the ten ccoef_*
  attributes (cv09), against the command's .stor, matbld's .stor and
  matbld's ccoef / ij_ccoef (cv_dual_tools/ccoef_check.py).

  Cases that must fail (er01 ... er03): an unknown keyword, avs, a bad
  value, no mesh object, an unknown one, an attribute name taken by an
  integer attribute, a ccoef_ij_* name taken by a real attribute, a
  hex mesh, a mesh that is not Delaunay (with
  Voronoi; cv median then goes on).

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_control_volume.py)

  ran        LaGriT ran the whole deck (after.inp exists)
  errors     the number of "ERROR: dump/control_volume" lines
  message    each text cases.txt names is in LaGriT's output
  nothing    no file named bad* (the failing commands' outputs)
  files      the command wrote the same files as the program, no other
  bytes      every file equal byte for byte, the .stor's line 2 aside
  line2      the .stor's line 2 ends with (cv_dual dump /
             control_volume / MO / ...), the command
  screen     the program's lines appear, in order, in LaGriT's output
             (cv_dual's lines go to LaGriT's log)
  attribute  the attribute is in after.inp and equals the .stor's
             volumes in every digit; with none asked for, after.inp has
             the same attributes as mesh.inp

  The meshes come from other suites: test_cv_dual_dfn
  (full_mesh.inp), test_cv_dual_parity (two_mat.inp),
  test_cv_dual_poisson_lagrit (test_3d_poi_01.inp) and
  test_cv_dual_delaunay's generator (flip3d.inp, made in work/gen).

WHAT WAS FOUND (Nov 17 2026)

  - LaGriT's log writes each line with (a80): a shorter line comes out
    at the right, and a longer one is cut at column 80 with the rest
    at the right. The command sends cv_dual's lines in an 80-column
    (or longer) buffer, and keeps its own lines within 80 columns.
  - settets / parents on a mesh read from AVS made no parents (itp1
    stays 0); after connect with an interface surface it makes them.
    After resetpts / parent the children are dudded vertices in no
    cell (cv_dual gives them volume 0 and a warning); rmpoint /
    compress removes them. cv_dual's message names both commands.

